name:Oratio Réspice (after Super ómnia);
office-part:Oratio;
book:Text Missale O.P. (1939), p. 177; inflexion marks (flex sign and colons) from Officium Hebdomadæ Sanctæ / Triduum O.P. (1927), p. 205;
commentary:Set to the Dominican tone for orations at Vespers, Lauds and Mass (Processionarium O.P. 1913, pp. 404-406). Rubric: "Antiphona finita ... dicat sequentem Orationem, sine Dóminus vobíscum et sine Orémus, Fratribus super formas prostratis" (Missal p. 177), Triduum p. 205 adds "sicut dicitur ad horas hujus diei" and ends it with the flex sign;
